WEBVTT

NOTE Opportunity: The Last Signal. AI-generated voice-over (ElevenLabs), transcribed by AIRXON.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.510
What can another world
teach us about our own?

2
00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:07.850
For decades, humanity
has looked toward Mars,

3
00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:11.390
searching for answers hidden
in its ancient landscape.

4
00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:17.650
A world of ancient rocks, vast
plains, and unanswered questions.

5
00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:22.610
A world that would require an
extraordinary machine to explore.

6
00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:28.360
Meet Opportunity, a robotic
explorer built by NASA

7
00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:31.900
to investigate the red
planet and uncover clues

8
00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:34.930
about its ancient environmental history.

9
00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:39.660
In 2003, Opportunity
began a journey that would

10
00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:42.750
carry it millions of
kilometers away from Earth.

11
00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:46.740
Inside its spacecraft,
Opportunity traveled

12
00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:49.500
through the darkness
of interplanetary space

13
00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:52.510
toward a world waiting to be explored.

14
00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:56.230
Reaching Mars was only the beginning.

15
00:00:56.860 --> 00:00:59.340
Opportunity had to
survive the challenge of

16
00:00:59.380 --> 00:01:02.090
landing on an entirely different world.

17
00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:08.170
Opportunity reached Meridiani Planum
and began investigating the terrain,

18
00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:10.590
one observation at a time.

19
00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:16.100
Every movement across the terrain
helped scientists investigate a world

20
00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:18.670
they could never explore directly.

21
00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:22.320
Using specialized scientific instruments,

22
00:01:22.360 --> 00:01:25.570
Opportunity examined rocks and soil,

23
00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:28.370
gathering evidence
about the planet's past.

24
00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:32.190
The rocks revealed
something extraordinary,

25
00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:37.650
evidence that ancient environments
on Mars had once contained water.

26
00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:41.440
Among its findings were
tiny mineral formations

27
00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:44.540
and geological clues
that helped scientists

28
00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:47.910
reconstruct Mars's environmental history.

29
00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:52.710
Designed to operate for
just 90 Martian sols,

30
00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:56.350
Opportunity continued
working for nearly 15 years,

31
00:01:56.740 --> 00:01:59.970
a mission far beyond its
original expectations.

32
00:02:01.160 --> 00:02:07.170
Then came 2018, a massive global
dust storm enveloped Mars,

33
00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:11.090
changing the conditions under
which Opportunity operated.

34
00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:15.340
The dust blocked sunlight from
reaching its solar panels,

35
00:02:15.380 --> 00:02:19.270
threatening the energy required
to keep the rover operating.

36
00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:25.550
After its final communication, NASA
continued efforts to restore contact.

37
00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:28.830
But Opportunity never responded again.

38
00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:33.710
Opportunity's mission ended,
but its discoveries remain.

39
00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:37.940
Across the silence of
Mars, its journey continues

40
00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:41.750
to inspire our exploration
of worlds beyond Earth.
